    "answer": "Otto's spec (FR-003 of support-agent-escalation) says a switch over every EscalationTrigger member with no default was the intended check. Adding a member without a matching case would then fail `npm run typecheck`. As built, the fixture `apps/api/test/fixtures/escalationTriggers.ts` is a `Record<EscalationTrigger, TriggerSource>` checked through a `satisfies` clause. There are two reasons. A Record fails typecheck the same way: a member added without an entry is an error, and so is an extra member. And a switch covering all ten triggers would exceed the lint complexity limit. Each PR that adds a trigger updates the fixture in the same PR, so typecheck shows the member was handled.",
